# Google OAuth client ID for the optional read-only Google Calendar sync
# (see ARCHITECTURE.md §7, "Google Calendar integration"). Create one at
# https://console.cloud.google.com/apis/credentials as an "OAuth client ID"
# of type "Web application", with your dev origin (e.g. http://localhost:5173)
# and your deployed origin (e.g. https://<user>.github.io) added under
# "Authorized JavaScript origins". This ID is not secret — it's meant to be
# embedded in client-side apps — but it's specific to your Google Cloud
# project, so it isn't committed here.
#
# Copy this file to .env.local (gitignored via *.local) for local dev, and
# set the same value as a repository variable named VITE_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID
# for the GitHub Pages build (see .github/workflows/deploy.yml).
VITE_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=
